# Environment / secrets
# `.env` alone left sibling files exposed — a `.env.bak`, `.env.local`, or
# `.env.prod` was fully trackable and one `git add .` from being committed.
# The negation keeps the (deliberately tracked, placeholder-only) .env.example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

